# HBM4 timing profile TEMPLATE — fill from a vendor datasheet.
#
# Structure: JESD270-4A Table 108 ("Timings Parameters") and Table 3
# ("Array Access Timings Counted Individually Per Pseudo Channel").
# JESD270-4A leaves the core array timing VALUES vendor-defined (the
# min/max columns are blank in the standard) — only the values marked
# "spec-fixed" below come from the standard itself. Everything marked
# FILL_ME needs a real product datasheet (SK hynix / Samsung / Micron).
#
# To use: copy to hbm4-<vendor>-<part>.csv in this directory, replace
# every FILL_ME, delete rows that don't apply, and drop the .example
# suffix — the unit suite auto-discovers and load-tests every *.csv
# here, which is why this template is NOT a .csv itself.
#
# Loader notes (jedec_timings.py):
#   - The first 15 rows are the loader's REQUIRED set; the HBM4-native
#     symbols they map to are named in each description.
#   - Rows after the required set load as `extras` — keep the HBM4
#     split-parameter detail there (RD/WR RCD split, L/S RRD, ab/pb
#     RFC) even though the state model consumes the merged values.
#   - Per Table 3, the array-access timings count INDIVIDUALLY PER
#     PSEUDO CHANNEL; the DFI BFM models one pseudo channel per
#     profile instance.

parameter,   unit, value,   description
tCK,         ns,   FILL_ME, DFI clock period for the modeled speed grade
tRCD,        ns,   FILL_ME, ACT to RD delay — HBM4 tRCDRD (use the read value; tRCDWR goes in extras)
tRP,         ns,   FILL_ME, PRECHARGE command period (tRP)
tRAS_min,    ns,   FILL_ME, ACT to PRE minimum (tRAS; spec-fixed max = 9 x tREFI)
tRC,         ns,   FILL_ME, ACT to ACT same bank (tRC)
tWR,         ns,   FILL_ME, WRITE recovery (tWR)
tWTR,        ns,   FILL_ME, WRITE to READ turnaround — HBM4 tWTRL (tWTRS in extras)
tRTP,        ns,   FILL_ME, READ to PRECHARGE same bank (tRTP; spec gives nCK — convert)
tRRD,        ns,   FILL_ME, ACT to ACT different bank — HBM4 tRRDL (tRRDS in extras)
tFAW,        ns,   FILL_ME, Four-bank activate window (tFAW)
tREFI,       ns,   3900,    Average refresh interval — spec-fixed 3.9 us (JESD270-4A section 6.9)
tRFC,        ns,   FILL_ME, Refresh cycle time — HBM4 tRFCab (tRFCpb in extras)
CL,          CK ,  FILL_ME, Read latency RL for the speed grade
CWL,         CK ,  FILL_ME, Write latency WL for the speed grade
BL,          beats, FILL_ME, Burst length (HBM4 prefetch)
# --- HBM4-native detail (loads as extras) -----------------------------
tRCDWR,      ns,   FILL_ME, ACT to WR delay (Table 108 tRCDWR)
tRRDS,       ns,   FILL_ME, ACT to ACT different bank group (tRRDS)
tWTRS,       ns,   FILL_ME, WRITE to READ different bank group (tWTRS)
tRTW,        ns,   FILL_ME, READ to WRITE turnaround (tRTW)
tCCDL,       CK ,  FILL_ME, CAS to CAS same bank group (tCCDL)
tCCDS,       CK ,  FILL_ME, CAS to CAS different bank group (tCCDS)
tCCDR,       CK ,  FILL_ME, CAS to CAS different pseudo channel (tCCDR)
tRFCpb,      ns,   FILL_ME, Per-bank refresh cycle time (tRFCpb)
tREFIPB,     ns,   FILL_ME, Per-bank refresh interval (tREFIPB)
tRREFD,      ns,   FILL_ME, REFpb to REFpb different bank (tRREFD)
tPPD,        CK ,  2,       PRE to PRE same pseudo channel — spec-fixed (Table 108)
tCKSRX,      CK ,  5,       Valid clocks before SELF REFRESH EXIT — spec-fixed (Table 108)
